# Dot UI rule (Presentation layer, .NET UI apps)
Base rule: .cursor/rules/dot.mdc.
- Clean Architecture; Presentation (Views/ViewModels) holds NO business logic. Domain→Application→Infrastructure→Presentation.
- Structure: Assets/ (Fonts, Images, Styles), Components/, Pages|Views/ (by feature), ViewModels/ (with Base/), Services/ (Navigation, Dialog), Converters/.
- Naming: Views `[Feature]Page|Window|View`; `[Feature]ViewModel`; `I[Name]Service`; `[Action]Command`; async `[Method]Async`. Root namespace `DotApps.<AppName>`.
- Design: Fluent 2 — Mica/Acrylic, shadows/strokes, motion, Segoe UI Variable, Light/Dark.
- On UI/Presentation/Fluent 2 conflicts, this rule wins. Don't duplicate base dot rules here.
